\section{Introduction}
\label{sec:intro}

HTTP adaptive streaming dominates Internet video delivery: MPEG-DASH/HLS players fetch chunked segments while a client-side \emph{adaptive bitrate} (ABR) controller selects discrete representations each chunk period~\cite{sodagar2011mpeg,bentaleb2018survey}.
Stalls remain acutely perceptible and quality instability is distracting, yet mobile deployments---especially sub-6~GHz/mmWave heterogeneous access---expose clients to outages, blockage, LOS/NLOS swings, scheduler bursts, and path changes that abruptly collapse achievable throughput~\cite{wu2024qoe,cisco2023,meng2024mmwave}.
In trace suites biased toward stabilized backbone emulation, reinforcement-learning prototypes such as Pensieve~\cite{mao2017neural} can present impressive average surrogates.
\textbf{Outside that comfort zone lies the pragmatic failure mode:} learned policies tuned on comparatively smooth workloads may behave \textit{bitrate-greedy} when capacity suddenly tightens from cellular volatility, reallocating playback time probability into rare but disastrous \textit{tail stalls} that scalar rewards systematically under-weigh~\cite{sutton2018reinforcement,yan2019learning}.

Layered safeguards help: augment constraint-aware learning with deterministic \textit{runtime shielding}---action projection onto buffer-feasible choices immediately before fetching the next chunk~\cite{alshiekh2018shielding}.
\textbf{However, predominant shield formulations are perceptually uninformed.}
When risk tests fire they almost always execute \textit{content-blind} \textbf{representation-index decrements}: move one bitrate step down irrespective of whether that step slashes VMAF disproportionately~\cite{li2016vmaf}.
Because ladders are perceptually nonlinear, naive decrements are rarely ``visually proportional'' sacrifices; operators therefore inherit an opaque folklore trade-off (\emph{stay safe $\Rightarrow$ accept whatever ugliness decrement-hopping inflicts}), even though many emergencies admit safer ladder paths with tiny perceptual loss.
\textbf{Research gap:} projection rules are seldom treated as first-class perceptual optimization problems atop nonlinear ladders~\cite{xiao2025qoe,tian2022towards}.

\textbf{Our positioning --- from compromise to empirical strict Pareto.}
We reposition streaming control as a CMDP instantiated with primal--dual Lagrangian PPO~\cite{altman1999constrained,paternain2019dual,schulman2017proximal,achiam2017constrained} and augment it with what we contend is absent in shield practice: \textbf{a VMAF-aware runtime shield family} parameterized by perceptual-loss tolerance $\tau$ and catastrophic-ratio $\rho_{\mathrm{cat}}$ (Sec.~\ref{sec:method:shield}), replacing blind index ladders with VMAF-guided projection subject to viability tests~\cite{alshiekh2018shielding,li2016vmaf}.
Relative to ubiquitous legacy projection~\cite{mao2017neural,alshiekh2018shielding}, paired replay establishes \textit{simultaneously} larger mean QoE, lower mean rebuffering, and higher mean VMAF on the FCC/Norway-style partitioned suite standard in trace-driven ABR research (paired Wilcoxon, $n{=}\VNepisodes$; Sec.~\ref{sec:eval})---i.e.\ a statistically witnessed \textit{strict} three-way improvement, not merely negotiating another QoE--stall knob.
\textbf{Synthetic low-latency 5G/mmWave stress replay} corroborates that pattern under outage-heavy OOD regimes: VMAF-aware projection retains large QoE lifts and statistically significant stall reductions versus legacy shields (Sec.~\ref{sec:eval:ood}), while paired VMAF separation saturates whenever sessions stall-dominantly, underscoring honest dimension-wise reporting~\cite{lakens2018equivalence,meng2024mmwave}.
Meanwhile, collapsing $\VShieldVariants$ probes to $\VShieldBehaviors$ behavioral classes exposes the VMAF-aware fallback—not threshold-only tweaks—as the Pareto driver, and stripping shields from shield-co-trained policies inflates stalls ($|\VPairedDRbvsOff|\,\%$, $p{=}\VPairedPRbvsOff$), proving \textit{policy--shield co-design} is not rhetoric.

\textbf{Trust and operational deployability.}
Neural bitrate policies seldom ship without operator anxiety: function approximators are black boxes lacking universal formal guarantees~\cite{sutton2018reinforcement,mao2017neural}.
\textbf{Shield layers supply auditability orthogonal to RL expressivity:}
interventions are deterministic functions of observable manifest metadata, pessimistic throughput estimates, buffer occupancy, VMAF ladders, $\tau$, and $\rho_{\mathrm{cat}}$; each adjustment logs an auditable flag.
\textbf{Scope of formal claims:}
we do not certify worst-case QoE for arbitrary future stacks; we instead pair measurable deterministic guards with transparent statistics under published trace-driven emulation norms~\cite{meng2024mmwave,yan2019learning}.

\textbf{Technical note.}
Beyond CMDP+PPO wrappers we reuse manifest lookahead features~\cite{sodagar2011mpeg}; optional Lyapunov-motivated cues remain heuristic drift dampers~\cite{neely2010stochastic,chow2018lyapunov}.

This paper contributes, relative to MPC ABR~\cite{yin2015control}, Pensieve-era DRL ABR~\cite{mao2017neural,gadaleta2017ddash}, and safety-flavored streaming RL~\cite{xiao2025qoe,tian2022towards}:
\begin{enumerate}
  \item \textbf{A Lagrangian CMDP+PPO end-to-end stack} with dual updates over smoothed stall and switching surrogates atop future-aware Pensieve-class inputs.

  \item \textbf{To our knowledge, the first VMAF-aware runtime shield in this trace-driven benchmarking harness}, which replaces content-blind index decrements with ladder-respecting perceptual downgrade and auditable catastrophe tests (Sec.~\ref{sec:method:shield}).

  \item \textbf{Strict Pareto evidence plus 5G-style stress corroboration.} FCC/Norway-style paired replay statistically validates triple QoE/Rebuffer/VMAF dominance over legacy projection (paired Wilcoxon signed-rank, $n{=}\VNepisodes$, Sec.~\ref{sec:eval}); synthetic mmWave blockage stress traces reaffirm QoE/Rebuffer superiority versus legacy shields under heavy outage regimes (Sec.~\ref{sec:eval:ood})~\cite{meng2024mmwave}.

  \item \textbf{A structural characterization and deployment imperative.} Controlled sweeps collapse to $\VShieldBehaviors$ classes isolating VMAF-aware projection as decisive, while shield omission catastrophically rewires inferred safety~\cite{alshiekh2018shielding}, arguing shields must accompany deployment builds.
\end{enumerate}

\textbf{Paper roadmap.}
Section~\ref{sec:related} contrasts classical, MPC, learning-based ABR streams with constrained RL and shield metaphors.
Section~\ref{sec:system} formalizes surrogate QoE, CMDP constraints, shield interfaces, throughput-driven simulation abstractions.
Section~\ref{sec:method} documents Lagrangian PPO wrappers, shield pseudocode/training interplay, VMAF-guided projection, catastrophe logic, knobs, and reproducibility freezes.
Section~\ref{sec:eval} answers research questions via tables, statistical tests, and visuals including partitioned backbone traces plus supplementary 5G/mmWave outage stress.
Sections~\ref{sec:limits}--\ref{sec:conclusion} discuss threats (\emph{e.g.,} emulation versus live deployments) and distill closing guidance.

