\textbf{Headline finding (RQ1).}
On the FCC/Norway-style primary suite (\(n{=}\VNepisodes\) paired episodes), the headline result is a \emph{strict three-way Pareto improvement} of the VMAF-aware shield over the standard index-decrement (legacy) projection, on the same trained policy and identical trace seeds. Holding the catastrophic-ratio knob fixed and toggling only the VMAF-aware fallback projection, mean session QoE increases by \VPairedDQoEvsLeg, mean rebuffering decreases by $|\VPairedDRbvsLeg|\,\%$, and mean VMAF increases by \VPairedDVMvsLeg{} simultaneously (paired Wilcoxon, $p{=}\VPairedPQoEvsLeg$ for QoE, $p{=}\VPairedPRbvsLeg$ for rebuffer). Tightening the VMAF-loss tolerance from $1.0$ to $0.8$ widens the win to \VPairedDQoEvsLegStr\, paired $\Delta$QoE, $\VPairedDRbvsLegStr\,\%$ rebuffering, and $+\VPairedDVMvsLegStr$ VMAF---all three metrics improving simultaneously with statistical significance. To the best of our knowledge, no prior ABR shield reports a strict three-way Pareto improvement of this form on comparable paired harnesses.

\textbf{(OOD stress traces.)}
Section~\ref{sec:eval:ood} repeats the replay under synthetic 5G/mmWave outages; QoE gains and stall reductions versus the legacy shield remain paired-significant (e.g., \(\tau{=}1.0\): \(\VFiveGPairedDQoEten\) $\Delta$QoE with \(p{=}\VFiveGPairedPQoEten\); \(\VFiveGPairedDRbten\,\%\) points $\Delta$rebuffer with \(p{=}\VFiveGPairedPRbten\)). Mean VMAF is not reliably separated (\(p=\VFiveGPairedPVmten\) at \(\tau{=}1.0\)), which we interpret as limited statistical power once average session VMAF collapses toward a stall-dominated plateau rather than contradictory evidence relative to Table~\ref{tab:pareto:family}.

Table~\ref{tab:pareto:family} reports the full sweep. The VMAF-aware family (rows 2--5) Pareto-dominates the legacy anchor on QoE, rebuffering, \emph{and} VMAF concurrently. By contrast, threshold-only sweeps that vary $\rho_{\mathrm{cat}}$ \emph{without} the VMAF-aware fallback (the third block of the table) move QoE up by smaller, statistically non-significant margins while \emph{worsening} rebuffering by $2$--$5$ percentage points (Section~\ref{sec:eval:shields} details). This isolates the VMAF-aware fallback as the active Pareto driver: it is the \emph{shape} of the projection rule, not the threshold itself, that bends the front.

